{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex","id":1270044,"title":"Rivals to Pentex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-23T01:09:49-08:00","id":1270044,"title":"Rivals to Pentex","content":"So I\u2019ve got a hankering for options. Just like we need more magical Martial Artists then just Akashics (I\u2019ll get to that in another thread) we need more evil weird multi billion dollar Corporations then just Pentex!<br /> <br /> So yes we have Pentex.<br /> D.N.A<br /> The Giovanni and Friends spread out<br /> Ventrue Spread out<br /> SYNDICATE<br /> Zaibatsu<br /> <br /> <br /> So I want to add a company drawing on themes from Marvels Exxon Fuel Company and FF7\u2019s Shinra Electric. I got a plan to tie in some other weird Billinaires like King Jupiter Industries, who I\u2019ll ise for some underground entertainment, after they made it big with the Worlds first Reality TV Lifestream the Max Jupiter Show (blatant rip-off if the Truman Show). <br /> <br /> But the Energy company I want will, like Roxxon, make plans to Plunder Other realms ( like Dreaming, Umbra, The Underworld) for reasources, and also work to plunder the worlds sacred places, like Shinra, for power. People more knowledgeable then I can you tell me how easily will it be to cover up producing Billions of dollars worth of Energy and materials? Like camouflaging it as normal earthly mines and oil reserves or patented yet super secret zero point energy engines or something? How well can they cover up they get it from a supernatural source. I figure Syndicate knows and probably some have fingers in the pie like with Pentex. But tapping energy from the Umbra, or using SCIENCE to convert emphemera into minerals, how well can you hide producing that if you cheat ruuuuully good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T11:19:29-08:00","id":1270152,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of having competing rival mule-national corporations. Its a theme that pops up very often and has great potential for gaming. Players could be working for one against the others, they could be playing them against each other, or maybe just trying to bring down the entire system. <br /> <br /> I also quite like the idea of a ostensibly &quot;good guy&quot; corporation that may be forced to make more and more compromising decisions in order to combat they opposition, maybe a Glass Walkers ran company for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24609-edd123","name":"edd123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T12:06:43-08:00","id":1270163,"title":"","content":"Executive Outreach, Japanese Corporation Run by The Yama King Mikaboshi.<br /> <br /> The Teiai corporation-a Banking conglomerate that functions as a go between for various jaded supernatural types and the mundane. It is here you can trade in books, dross, or other supernatural favors for the &quot;mundane&quot; requirements to setup a secret temple underground or a gambling ring where you watch people hopelessly in debt fight to the death or whatever else your supernatural being with too much power and a bit of boredom wants to have done. Because someone has to sponsor all those underground deathgames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T12:10:08-08:00","id":1270166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>edd123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1270152#post1270152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also quite like the idea of a ostensibly &quot;good guy&quot; corporation that may be forced to make more and more compromising decisions in order to combat they opposition, maybe a Glass Walkers ran company for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies had one of these. But I don't remember the name. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T14:43:22-08:00","id":1270201,"title":"","content":"The shinzui corporation is would be easy to setup as a rival of Pentex. They work for the weaver in the same way Pentex works for the wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T16:37:30-08:00","id":1270224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1270201#post1270201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shinzui corporation is would be easy to setup as a rival of Pentex. They work for the weaver in the same way Pentex works for the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that rings a bell was it in book of the weaver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T19:18:27-08:00","id":1270248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex#post1270044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I want to add a company drawing on themes from Marvels Exxon Fuel Company</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean Roxxon Oil. Exxon is a real world company.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Roxxon is one of the influences for PENTEX and Endron, as one of their 1970s storylines involved their Board of Directors being under the control of the Serpent Crown, the artifact which allowed primordial serpent god Set (not to be confused with the Egyptian one) an anchor into Earth's dimension after he and the other Old Ones were driven out by Demiurge the Godeater.<br /> <br /> Elsewhere, IIRC, there are a couple of Asian companies mentioned in some post-Hengeyokai sourcebooks for Werewolf (Book of the Weaver, IIRC, and some others.)<br /> <br /> There should probably be some sort of Weaver counterpart to PENTEX, one based on the recent activities of companies like Facebook, Google, and the like. The new Patriarch is not based on religion, but on social conformity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Added: One of the more obscure companies is Arashikage Consumer Products, a Hakken-owned company mentioned in Mage's Dragons of the East. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-24-2018, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T19:30:15-08:00","id":1280032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1270166#post1270166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummies had one of these. But I don't remember the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ashukhi, and at the time that Resurrection came out, Ashukhi were a strong company, but not powerful enough to stand against Pentex. It's reasonable to assume that they could have grown to the point of having subsidiaries on their own, but that's a logical conclusion based on the passage of time and the assumption that the Glasswalkers don't destroy them for being a company full of mummies, which makes them enemies of Gaia no matter how much good they try to do. That statement isn't out of the blue, either. Leila Veil Shredder wanted Ashukhi to ship products for her company, Omni-Med, but Ashukhi Hoshi, the head of Ashukhi, refuses to do business with her, because he picks up on her Rage and doesn't trust her. Someone like Leila would look into the company after that, and being an Elder Glasswalker, there's no way that they can hide their secrets from her. She would certainly do everything in her power to eradicate Ashukhi as a corporation. Now, if she decided against it for some unexplainable reason, yes, Ashukhi could by now have subsidiaries. I don't see ANY new player ever getting strong enough to oppose Pentex, though. Further, they'd have to find out about Pentex and what they're doing. That's a tall order of not likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T02:43:03-08:00","id":1280073,"title":"","content":"I long ago adapted Destro and his MARS company from GIJoe into an Iteration X controlled company that had existed for several hundred years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T05:55:57-08:00","id":1280085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1280032#post1280032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ashukhi, and at the time that Resurrection came out, Ashukhi were a strong company, but not powerful enough to stand against Pentex. It's reasonable to assume that they could have grown to the point of having subsidiaries on their own, but that's a logical conclusion based on the passage of time and the assumption that the Glasswalkers don't destroy them for being a company full of mummies,which makes them enemies of Gaia no matter how much good they try to do. </div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the name.<br /> <br /> However, mummies enemies of Gaia?, the Silent Striders didn't seem to believe that when they formed part of the Osirian League. Do you think that the Glaswalkers would prove to be more close-minded and harder to approach than the Striders?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T15:22:00-08:00","id":1280188,"title":"","content":"Hmm. A Giovanni allience of family controlled companies such textile mills, firearm manufacturers, insurance companies, hospitals, shipping companies, casinos, porn productions, private security companies, private prisons, and the like. Under the umbrella of Augustus Investments.<br /> <br /> A Weaver version of PENTEX would, I think, be focused on things like public and private education, medical research and biotechnology, social media platforms and web engines, behavioral research, pharmaceuticals, alternative energy, and news media.<br /> <br /> ADDED: I wonder if calling such a company ACME would be too silly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-14-2019, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T21:18:47-08:00","id":1280251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1280085#post1280085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the name.<br /> <br /> However, mummies enemies of Gaia?, the Silent Striders didn't seem to believe that when they formed part of the Osirian League. Do you think that the Glaswalkers would prove to be more close-minded and harder to approach than the Striders?.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should read the *revised* (aka latest) version of the Silent Strider Tribe Book. They make it very clear that mummies are an affront to Gaia, because the dead are meant to be dead, and they exist because of a perverted ritual that tricked the Wyrm of Balance into allowing what is against nature itself. Yeah, mummies are creatures of balance, but that doesn't mean that Garou have to see it that way. The same book that I mention does contract itself to a degree, but the overall thing that you get if you read the various TINY blurbs about the Undying, is that they're one of the top 4 enemies of the Tribe, but LAST on their list, because they seem to cause no harm, that SOME Silent Striders will willingly work with them, and that most Garou that become familiar with them despise them. <br /> <br /> As for Glasswalkers, I think that any Glasswalker Elder who is snubbed by some pencil-neck, who is then found out to be a mummy and whose company is found to have the creatures, is going to be a serious threat to them. I see them very likely making dismantling of the company a priority, but this is all speculation off of what I read. It's logical conclusions, or at least *I* think that it's logical. You are free not to agree with that assessment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T13:24:44-08:00","id":1281358,"title":"","content":"For amusement...<br /> <b>Augustus Investments</b>, created in the 1950s as a financial investment firm and holding company for the intelligent and discreet investor. In truth, the bulk of their investors are from the tangled web of Giovanni families around the world and their investments are primarily into Giovanni family owned companies. However, they do like to lure in outside investors as a method of influence gathering, and will at times invest money in anything that looks like it will turn a prophet. Some of their holdings include:<ul><li><b>Schwarzstahl</b>, nominally a German based industrial company, they're actually a weapons manufacturing concern dating back to the 18th century. Students of corporate history are still unable to figure out how they survived the war crimes tribunals after WW2, and today they make automotive and truck parts, industrial chemicals, high grade medical instruments, light military vehicles, and firearms. They were founded by and continue to be controlled by the Koenigs.</li> <li><b>The Grand Augustus</b>, an imperial Roman themed mega casino in Las Vegas that rakes in massive amounts of money each year, both from gambling and from its wide range of entertainment venues. Strangely, the casino seems to have a higher than average staff turnover, as a number of young employees drawn to the city from small towns across the west seem to disappear without a trace. Initially funded and managed by the Rothsteins.</li> <li><b>Gardner Farms</b>, an agribusiness based in Massachusetts specializing in high priced organic produce, including cranberries, squash, mushrooms, apples, and heirloom potatoes. Owned by a smaller branch of the Milliners, there's nothing apparently wrong with the food. But visitors to their farms describe a sense of unease, sometimes bordering on creepiness.</li> <li><b>Lacrime</b>, an Italian fashion house famed for its original designs hip ready to wear fashions, as well as their top notch leather goods. Rumor has it that if one has enough money and the right in with the company, they can have exquisite custom made leather items crafted from &quot;special&quot; materials. The company is the passion project of a Giovanni ancilla.</li> <li><b>Corazon Clinics</b>, a series of health clinics primarily based in poor urban areas and Latino neighborhoods in the US and Mexico, offering relatively low cost (and often no-questions asked) medical care. Where they really make their money is through harvesting and selling human organs on the black market. It also provides the Pisonob family with human sacrifices for their Aztec rituals.</li> <li><b>Deadline Press</b>, a small press comic book publisher which got it's start in mid-80s Edinburgh, and currently sells books in Europe, North American and Australia. Originally heavily inspired by books like Heavy Metal, Warrior and 2000AD, much of their current work is infamous for hyper-sexualized extreme violence and main characters who could most charitably be described as sociopathic a-holes intoxicated by their own sense of hip moral superiority. Originally founded by Garp Dunsirn, a comic writer who became much more known for his obnoxious online personality (this in the days before Twitter, which is saying something) than for his actual work.</li> <li><b>Yin Gu Exchange</b>, a San Francisco based import/export company specializing in goods from China and Southeast Asia. In addition to the usual assortment of cheep tourist bate, food products, and clothing, they also smuggle antiques, counterfeit goods and people. Run by the Li Weng.</li> <li><b>Automobili Romano SpA</b>, makers of ultra-high-end luxury sports cars (and more recently SUVs), including armored vehicles designed for diplomats, celebrities and crime lords.</li> </ul>(I'll probably add to this from time to time as the mood strikes me. Possibly some ACME stuff too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-29-2019, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T16:37:55-08:00","id":1281841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1281358#post1281358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For amusement...<br /> <b>Augustus Investments</b>, created in the 1950s as a financial investment firm and holding company for the intelligent and discreet investor. In truth, the bulk of their investors are from the tangled web of Giovanni families around the world and their investments are primarily into Giovanni family owned companies. However, they do like to lure in outside investors as a method of influence gathering, and will at times invest money in anything that looks like it will turn a prophet. Some of their holdings include:</div> </div> </div> </div>You always have a great mind for how nasty things work in the WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T16:48:44-07:00","id":1343885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1280188#post1280188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if calling such a company ACME would be too silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it wouldn't. One of my NPCs was a CEO of Australian Computer Manufacturing Enterprise \ud83d\ude09.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T17:29:36-07:00","id":1343888,"title":"","content":"I've always thought that this was the answer to the Ventrue mystery of the &quot;Hidden Masters.&quot; There was no great conspiracy to thwart the clan, they just don't have a monopoly on the idea of supernatural businesspersons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 10-30-2019, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T02:57:37-07:00","id":1343946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1343888#post1343888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought that this was the answer to the Ventrue mystery of the &quot;Hidden Masters.&quot; There was no great conspiracy to thwart the clan, they just don't have a monopoly on the idea of supernatural businesspersons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that. And (what an irony) most of the Pentex products are harmless (except for a slight taint, just enough to distract Garou) and most of its employees are innocent humans, who just want to feed their families. And even in Board of Directors humans have majority of votes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-27-2019, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T14:35:22-07:00","id":1344070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1270224#post1270224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh that rings a bell was it in book of the weaver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shinzui Industries Also shows up in Apocalypse, at the Weaver Ascendant scenario, where it uses the Machine in order to take over Pentex","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T04:57:28-07:00","id":1344633,"title":"","content":"Montgomery &quot;Monty&quot; Coven a.k.a the new Mithras founded Syndexioi, a cybersecurity company which he use to fight with the Ventrue and to search Cainites with no particular sect allegiance. I think it makes Syndexioi Pentex and Technocracy rival either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T06:29:15-07:00","id":1344645,"title":"","content":"I'm the farthest thing from an expert on Mage lore, but don't several wings of the Technocracy also have a lot of front companies as part of their war to influence culture and consensus reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T06:51:57-07:00","id":1344647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1344645#post1344645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm the farthest thing from an expert on Mage lore, but don't several wings of the Technocracy also have a lot of front companies as part of their war to influence culture and consensus reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not many have been named, but yes, a number of Union cabals and chantries work as or under the auspices of some sort of front company that advances Union interests. Biotech, advertising, engineering, etc. I think the original Technocracy sourcebooks included a sample business front for each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T10:47:28-07:00","id":1344695,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a> yes. They do. Especially the Syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T12:40:10-07:00","id":1344721,"title":"","content":"To be honest many of NPCs have their own businesses. And if you ST agrees you could even create a starting character who owns a company so powerful that Pentex will target it for a next takeover.<br /> <br /> Edit. I've just found out that Pentex sometimes creates rivals for Pentex deliberately. For example NikNak Computers (a rival of Sunburst).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-31-2019, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:20:04-07:00","id":1388999,"title":"","content":"There is of course the firm &quot;Crucible Genetics Amalgamated&quot; (from the Halls of the Arcanum p93)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:49:30-07:00","id":1389042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1388999#post1388999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is of course the firm &amp;quot;Crucible Genetics Amalgamated&amp;quot; (from the Halls of the Arcanum p93)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh what was their deal? Alchemists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:04:55-07:00","id":1389393,"title":"","content":"As I recall the Syndicate had some collaboration with Pentex via the Special Projects division (which either allied with Pentex or went its own way.. or possibly both) and the Syndicate tries to keep this fact from leaking out given how it could impact their relations with the rest of the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> I suspect some really old Kindred (high end Elders, Methuselah) could probably control economic interests that might rival Pentex. Almost certainly an Antediluvian could if they were inclined to go that route.<br /> <br /> I think the issue is that Pentex is powerful because its so diversified from many elements (including ties to Mages as mentioned previously, but also Vampires like the Sabbat and other factions.) whereas alot of the other factions tend to be more singularly focused. If you could amass a similar coalition of like-minded companies it would be much easier to compete. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:20:58-07:00","id":1389640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1389042#post1389042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh what was their deal? Alchemists?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the main yes - but also experimenting on supernatural creatures.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:00:35-07:00","id":1391723,"title":"","content":"I think there's a lot of room to just make up new Wyrm-Corps. You come up with a regular business, have a bane pop up to the CEO/shareholder, and have the Bane offer... I don't know.. A Cancer cure/penis enlargement should the company deliberately do a bad thing. <br /> <br /> But, more to the point: <br /> Pentex has rivals in normal businesses, and normal businesses do evil shit for money. Being Wyrm influenced is both a pro and a con. Pro's being magical power, potential quality of life increases for the boss, an excuse to take the easy route... Cons being, well, you might just be sabotaging yourself, and you're attracting eco-terrorists. You don't need the Wyrm to be an Evil corperation. you don't need the weaver to be an evil corperation. And a thing with Evil corporations is, well, they might have shares in other evil corporations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:48:51-07:00","id":1392029,"title":"","content":"Totally agree with the points of MyWifeIsScary above. Corporations in the real world haven't needed supernatural evil compelling them to create and/or facilitate suffering, tragedy, and calamity. The Bottom Line\u2122 serves perfectly well to motivate people to such acts.<br /> <br /> I've often gone back and forth over how to use PENTEX. Ultimately I settle into having PENTEX be a shadowy holding company-conspiracy-oligarchal alliance with its various subsidiaries being more present to provide public faces and setting flavor.<br /> <br /> Also given how PENTEX is described as undercutting itself in service of its spiritual patrons, I think having it have plenty of financial rivals makes perfect sense, although the leading corporations aligning to create the best possible market for their own interests is even more likely.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of corporations will suffer from Weaver and Wyrm taint to some degree. However that's different from full fledged Weaver- &amp; Wyrm- Corps where the corporation is in a direct alliance with some spiritual entity.<br /> <br /> PENTEX might be the most common term for it but I've always considered them to simply be one particularly significant example of a far more widespread phenomena in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T09:54:58-07:00","id":1392580,"title":"","content":"Wayland Industries specializes in Bio-weapon research, advanced robotics, and artificial intelligence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:01:15-07:00","id":1392832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1392580#post1392580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wayland Industries specializes in Bio-weapon research, advanced robotics, and artificial intelligence</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you even try to be creative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:54:46-07:00","id":1392845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1392832#post1392832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you even try to be creative?</div> </div> </div> </div>not really, I went for an easy one in case someone had a game running and hadn't thought of something obvious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:53:49-07:00","id":1392867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1392029#post1392029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally agree with the points of MyWifeIsScary above. Corporations in the real world haven't needed supernatural evil compelling them to create and/or facilitate suffering, tragedy, and calamity. The Bottom Line\u2122 serves perfectly well to motivate people to such acts.<br /> <br /> I've often gone back and forth over how to use PENTEX. Ultimately I settle into having PENTEX be a shadowy holding company-conspiracy-oligarchal alliance with its various subsidiaries being more present to provide public faces and setting flavor.<br /> <br /> Also given how PENTEX is described as undercutting itself in service of its spiritual patrons, I think having it have plenty of financial rivals makes perfect sense, although the leading corporations aligning to create the best possible market for their own interests is even more likely.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of corporations will suffer from Weaver and Wyrm taint to some degree. However that's different from full fledged Weaver- &amp; Wyrm- Corps where the corporation is in a direct alliance with some spiritual entity.<br /> <br /> PENTEX might be the most common term for it but I've always considered them to simply be one particularly significant example of a far more widespread phenomena in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agree. In my games Pentex is almost unbeatable because basically it doesn't do anything evil. Of course it could even loose financially to hurt Mother Gaia (they will compensate the losses by using it's factories in Scar) but they cannot be accused of any wrongdoings. P. ex. some Pentex company has 3 times bigger car park than the others from this area (the production building is the same prefabricated ugly cube their competitors use only the car park is bigger). Why you ask? You propably know that many firms have transport fleet for their employees (buses etc.). Some other promote carpooling. This one doing the opposite: they give their employees bonuses for coming with their own cars not taking their colleagues. For example 10$ per month multiplied by number of free seats multiplied by engine capacity. Is it bad for environement? Certainly. Is it profitable? No, but it could be compensated. Is it illegal? I doubt it. Add bonuses for being a loyal Pentex subsidiaries customer (and they can be really really big):<br /> <br /> Simon A. Mann goes shopping to Herrick's after his shift at DFG. There he buys Avalon doll for his daughter, Tellus FPS and Sunburst mouse for his son and Vesuvius Publishing book for his other daughter. Then he buys King beer and Circinus cigarettes for himself, Pangloss lipstick for his wife. He knows that they are safe, Aesop Research Company tested them. To feed his family he buys some tuna from Hallahan fishing and Young&amp;Smith INC. bread and butter. He also buys new Rainbow tires for his car. He's a happy man, the discount is so big and he didn't even need to carry a big photo album with coupons. He's of course a proecological man: he packs his stuff to Good House paper bag and takes it to his electrically propelled Falcon Pathfinder. Kids are hungry so the happy family goes to O'Tooleys. Then he goes to the Endron Oil gas station. It's the tornado season so he needs some fuel for his emergency generator. He pays less because his salary comes to the Consolidex Worldwide bank account. After that they all visit his father, a legless Desert Storm veteran (his Nastrum fighter was shot down over Baghdad) in Autumn Health Management System nursing home. His father gets the care for free because Simon is a Vesuvius newspapers subscriber. They will also visit his other son. He is currently at Homogenic. He's gay and this is inexcusable sin for a true patriot's son (and Simon is a patriot, he fought for his country, so does his father and grandfather and of course he buys american). It's certainly that Spooky Tooth heavy metal band's fault. Maybe this new RPG from Black Dog will help him. Yes, he has four children, thanks to Conceptual Services. Then he goes home, build in the suburbs of Jackson, MS by High Quality Builders. He could afford it because there was Omni TV subscription bundle and thanks to the company he works for his electricity bill from Atlas is much lower. There he meets his buddy from the Army, Joseph Grant. They fought together during Iraqi Freedom. Joe is a gunsmith and he repaired Simon's old hunting rifle made by Herculean. He needs it cause there was some bear/Big Foot sightings nearby. He also notices that Ardus Waste Management took his trash finally. After a little workout with Dr. Veridan workout program (as any Serpent Brother and Tau Upsilon Phi member would do) and a dose of Magadon vitamine supplement he sits on a couch. &quot;This will be a good evening&quot; he thinks. First there will be a new episode of &quot;Concrete Dreams&quot; (Omni TV exclusive), then Friday Fight Night, pay per view Extreme Wrestling Warfare show, after that NASCAR (&quot;this new Endron Sponsored driver, car #77, Samuel Ross is the embodiement of American Dream; hope he won't kill himself on the track like those two last guys who forgot that this car is so fast&quot;) and then &quot;Slayer XIV&quot;, new Slaughterhouse horror. And if he won't fall asleep he could also watch Pigeon River Howlers concert on RED TV (he always liked bluegrass). &quot;Tomorrow I have to remember to send this month charity checks to Save Our Schools society and The Fellowship, they do so much good for every children in the States&quot;. Yup, this was a good day. And yes, Simon and his family could smell like Malfeas and still could be a normal, mortal family. Could you kill Simon, his wife Annie and his kids: Grace, Faith and little Johnny, Biff (Big Intimidating F*****g Fenrir)?<br /> <br /> My girlfriend says that you should watch &quot;99 Francs&quot; as an inspiration. She graduated Art School with major in applies art so she knows what she's talking about. And a Cini Minis commercial (I don't know if it is aired in your country), the one with canibalistic allusions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TGRf_UAGlDg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TGRf_UAGlDg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TGRf_UAGlDg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/TGRf_UAGlDg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And now use your imagination \ud83d\ude08.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":".  My girlfriend's suggestions 05-30-2020, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:54:56-07:00","id":1392868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1392845#post1392845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> not really, I went for an easy one in case someone had a game running and hadn't thought of something obvious</div> </div> </div> </div>Explanation accepted \ud83d\ude09.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T14:27:13-07:00","id":1392900,"title":"","content":"On some level Corday Records, a Toreador (propably) owned, Boston (propably) based recording company (from Vampire Storyteller's Screen 2nd edition) could be a rival to Registered Artist Worldwide (from Freak Legions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:29:44-07:00","id":1392976,"title":"","content":"another easy and obvious one is the SCP Foundation and it's numerous subsidies that make it a profitable business, strangely, they are the only organization that only has humans as their upper leadership. they prioritize capturing and containing or neutralizing the most dangerous supernatural beings or things first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:06:27-07:00","id":1393032,"title":"","content":"So things with Pentex subsidiaries and other evil wyrm companies. <br /> <br /> 1- A lot of the supernatural evil shit they do, they can't be caught. <br /> Pentex put evil stuff in their products. Banes, spiritual bad bad, occult messages, all -chaotic evil- style. <br /> The issue is, you can't test for &quot;banes&quot; using science. You can't find that. They'll never get into trouble for it, unless the Technocracy somehow prepare the world for working with this stuff (which they won't) <br /> A lot of the other Chaotic evil stuff can be blamed on individuals, like putting mystery meat into an O'tolley's burger, you might get some expensive lawsuits but you can't bring a subsidiary down.<br /> <br /> 2. A lot of the evil shit they do is legal. <br /> Toxic waste dump? Child labour? Human experiments? Institutional abuse? Just go lobby the goverment to make that stuff ok. <br /> <br /> 3. The only real evil stuff you can catch them out on is the stuff that everybody else does in the world of darkness... Tax evasion, money laundering, insider trading, excess pollution; Just bribe or lawyer your way out of it, only a few underfunded nutjobs will come at you for that kinda thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T06:32:13-07:00","id":1393072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1393032#post1393032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So things with Pentex subsidiaries and other evil wyrm companies. <br /> <br /> 1- A lot of the supernatural evil shit they do, they can't be caught. <br /> Pentex put evil stuff in their products. Banes, spiritual bad bad, occult messages, all -chaotic evil- style. <br /> The issue is, you can't test for &quot;banes&quot; using science. You can't find that. They'll never get into trouble for it, unless the Technocracy somehow prepare the world for working with this stuff (which they won't) <br /> A lot of the other Chaotic evil stuff can be blamed on individuals, like putting mystery meat into an O'tolley's burger, you might get some expensive lawsuits but you can't bring a subsidiary down.<br /> <br /> 2. A lot of the evil shit they do is legal. <br /> Toxic waste dump? Child labour? Human experiments? Institutional abuse? Just go lobby the goverment to make that stuff ok. <br /> <br /> 3. The only real evil stuff you can catch them out on is the stuff that everybody else does in the world of darkness... Tax evasion, money laundering, insider trading, excess pollution; Just bribe or lawyer your way out of it, only a few underfunded nutjobs will come at you for that kinda thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The thing is that Pentex is composed of about 30 lesser companies many of which in turn are composed of lesser companies. If one gets into trouble the rest will propably help it. They can be hurt (in White Wolf Magazine #39 was an adventure Night of Rage during which a Magadon factory could be destroyed), they can be caught doing something PROPABLY illegal (in Project Twilight adventure a young chemistry student is mentioned; he found some strange formulas in some of Pangloss products). I think that some parts of Pentex could be even brought down only to be acquired by other Pentex companies (white wolf wiki on Pentex subject mention that Harold&amp;Harold Mining was bought by Endron). Buying off Pentex is possible (in one of Apocalypse scenarios Pentex is bought by Weaver company). Destroying it? Not likely. You have to remember that almost any of Pentex companies is the third in the world on its field. So even Garou (and better, their Kinfolks) uses their stuff. And I think that most of their stuff is harmless (that's why Simon's family are mortals), they could create fomori if used too often and in combination with other Pentex products (like in &quot;Batman&quot;; the one by Burton, Siren Cosmetics products are an exception and I think it's wrong). They have (or should have) two little effects: the users are slightly tainted (mortals and Kinfolks alike) so Wyrm Sense is tingling and is overloaded (that's why cities smell Wyrm mostly) and could have side effects. Most Magadon products could cause dog allergy. The good thing of that is twofold: most of Garou friends use at least one of Magadon products, they start to scratch when Garou is near so they will try to avoid him and, because most people use them and also begin to scratch, Garou could be easily sigled out in a crowd. Look at Circinus cigarettes: they aren't more harmful than any others. But if you try to quit you most likely go to Smoker's Bane and that's where you could become Sicklung (Freak Legion). Besides creating world composed of fomori takes decades and will be too visible for Pentex standards <br /> <br /> 2. Highly unlikely. There is some level of corruption that even public opinion won't accept. But there are many ways legal (as with the car park I mentioned above) that could harm Gaia. Look at the example mentioned in Subsidiaries Pentex: Magadon builds a hospital in a poor region of Africa. People (even in The rest of the world) are happy. Than they say: <br /> &quot;We could build 10 more but your governement won't allow our friends from Harold &amp; Harold strip mining in your country. Those bastards! They don't want you to live comfortably&quot;.<br /> And after the next election a more Pentex friendly people will rule. Or there could even be a revolt. You also could read/watch &quot;Dogs of war&quot; for an inspiration. <br /> <br /> 3. Basically yes, but there are many ways Pentex could be harmful and legal (just like car park example). The only way it could be stopped is by the media. But even then it could be avoided. First of all Pentex products are almost neccesary in modern world. Second they have a good PR teams. Third they also fund Gaia Research Company (an &quot;independent&quot; PR/research company Pentex uses to bolster claims of civic responsibility) and some fringe, violent ecoterrorist to give Greenpeace, WWF and Children of Gaia a bad name. Fourth people in World of Darkness are pathetic apatic couch potatos (mostly... hell, just like IRL) who don't want to know and react. C'mon, how many of you send checks to some eco foundation? When was the last time you protest against something Gaia unfriendly thing, even by leaving a comment in the Web or sending a letter to the press? You helped by buing original W:tA products: 3% of profit was send to some wolf friends organization. And the last argument that could be used: Kathryn Mollett from Pentex Board of Directors can't lie. It makes her a perfect weapon in media (or an albost ultimate tool of Pentex destruction). Imagine a press conference in any world wide media (back to the car park example):<br /> <br /> &quot;Miss Mollett, why don't you use your own fleet to transport your employees? Also you discourage carpooling by giving financial bonuses to employees who rides to work alone? You know it's bad for environement.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes, I know. But it cannot determine the life of humanity. As we all know accidents happens. If we use mass transport or carpool our employees we could lost a few of them in such accident, even if temporarily. Then we need the new ones. Before they will learn they could make mistakes. And that means flawed products. Do you want to take pills made by experienced or unexperienced? And you know our standards are high. We allow of course our people to travel together. Also, to help keep our home clean we also have a discount for employees who wants to buy an electric propelled car.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't you buy it?<br /> This cars are of course from Falcon Motors. But they aren't popular because if you get one you will loose engine capacity multiplier. If you want more read the last part of Rage Across NY adventure ideas (the one with dr. Draggerunter show).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-31-2020, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:01:56-07:00","id":1393078,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking we could use some Billionaires and tech companies in Changeling. It would be trivially easy for say high ranking Sidhe.<br /> <br /> Do we have any mentioned in say Kindred of the East?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:32:53-07:00","id":1393086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1270044-rivals-to-pentex?p=1393078#post1393078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m thinking we could use some Billionaires and tech companies in Changeling. It would be trivially easy for say high ranking Sidhe.<br /> <br /> Do we have any mentioned in say Kindred of the East?</div> </div> </div> </div>As for KotE check Killing Streets. I remember my friend's campaign during which he used Triple Harmony Insurance Underwriters, a hi-tech startups. He said he took it from KS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T08:51:56-07:00","id":1393105,"title":"","content":"I think we also all forgot about Orpheus Group (now Lazarus Redux, once JDG Cryogenics), Terrel &amp; Squib and NextWorld. I think that they all could compete with Pentex on many fields (especially because Pentex once had Giovanni vampire among board of directors and, in turn, Orpheus had someone with experience at Magadon among their high ranking workers; I don't recall the name). And of course Shadowlands has so big potential to corrupt.<br /> <br /> There's also Hermetic Society of Swift Light, a corax owned courier firm. If you are really in need, you can check character templates from tribebooks/clanbooks/breedbooks etc. I believe I saw at least one company, complete with name and trade, owned by Giovanni (revised clanbook) and two small companies owned by premade characters from Alien Hunger.<br /> <br /> And if you use WoD based video games you could also add Genefex (I believe it's not Pentex owned, rather a company which runs transport hubs for other companies)and Fairday Manufacturing, both from Hunter games, Orsi International (A metalurgical company, in 1999 owned by count Orsi, old Ventrue Antitribu) from V:tM Redemption and SunCo Gasoline (propably a chain of gas stations, one of them serving as a heaven for Bertram Tung, a Nosferatu), Metalhead Industries, Megahurtz Computers and Empire Arms Hotels (among many others) from Bloodlines.","signature":